          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The recognition principle for finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+loop+spaces"} relative loop spaces
            states that, for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi N
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq N \lt \infty
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of a relative
            = succeed "-loop" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            = succeed "-connected" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo −
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (N-2,N-1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Swiss+cheese+operad"} Swiss cheese operad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮𝒞
                      %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{SC}_N
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} algebra over an operad
          %p
            The recognition principle for infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+loop+spaces"} relative loop spaces
            states that a pair of pointed topological spaces is of the homotopy type of a relative
            = succeed "-loop" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮𝒞
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo →
                        %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮𝒞
                      %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{SC}_\infty\coloneqq \colim_{N\to\infty}\mathcal{SC}_N
          %p
            These are relative versions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/May+recognition+theorem"} May recognition theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#May72"}> May 72
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#May74"} May 74
          %p
            The recognition principle for relative
            = succeed "-loop" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#VVieira2020"} Vieira 2020
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi N
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3\leq N\leq \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1,2
            if we assume the spaces connected. The general case for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
            was proved in (
            %a{:href => "#HLS16"}> Hoefel, Livernet, Stasheff 2016
            ). The unconnected case for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=2
            remains open.
          %p
            Notoriously the loop space functors that appear in these recognition theorems are not right adjoint, thus they cannot be proved as an equivalence of homotopy categories induced by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+bar+construction"} two-sided bar construction
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#VVieira2020"} Vieira 2020
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            that allow for the units and counits to exist only up to functorially determined resolutions, providing a natural model theoretical axiomatization of the essential elements of May’s original proof. For the full proof, homotopical versions of the concepts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent adjunction
            require similar generalizations. This is because we are interested in the homotopy subcategories of grouplike algebras and
            = succeed "-connected" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo −
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (N-2,N-1)
          %p
            Bellow the proof of the relative recognition of
            = succeed "-loop" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 3
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi N
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3\leq N\leq \infty
            using the machinery of idempotent quasiadjunctions in (
            %a{:href => "#VVieira2020"}> Vieira 2020
            ) is sketched.
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#VVieira2020"}> Vieira 2023
            ) idempotent quasiadjunctions were used to prove a recognition theorem of
            = succeed "-loop" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+spectra"} algebra spectra
            over commutative
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+isometries+operad"} linear isometries operad
            is compatible with the model theoretical machinery presented here.
          %h2#idempotent_weak_quillen_quasiadjunctions Idempotent weak Quillen quasiadjunctions
          %h3#weak_quillen_quasiadjunction Weak Quillen quasiadjunction
          %p To construct the unit and counit natural transformations of an adjuction between homotopy categories of model categories it suffices to construct a unit natural span and counit natural cospan at the model categories level, plus some additional compatibility conditions.
          %p
          #QsiAdjQuilFr.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#VVieira2020"}> Vieira 2020, Definition 2.1.1
              ) Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              be model categories. A weak Quillen quasiadjunction, or just quasiadjunction, between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                        %mo ,
                        %mi.mathscript ℱ
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo ⇌
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (S \dashv_{\ \mathscr{C},\mathscr{F}}\Lambda):\mathcal{T}\rightleftharpoons \mathcal{A},
            %p is a quadruple of functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mi.mathscript ℱ
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mi S
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathscr{C}:\mathcal{T} \to \mathcal{T}
                    ,\quad
                    \\mathscr{F}:\mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{A}
                    ,\quad
                    S:\mathcal{T} \to \mathcal{A}
                    ,\quad
                    \\Lambda:\mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{T}
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              the left quasiadjoint and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
              the right quasiadjoint, equipped with a natural span in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              and a natural cospan in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                    %mover
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi 𝒯
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi.mathscript ℱ
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %mover
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mo ∼
                    %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta':\mathscr{C}\xRightarrow{\sim} Id_{\mathcal{T}}
                    ,\quad
                    \\eta:\mathscr{C}\Rightarrow \Lambda S
                    ,\qquad
                    \\epsilon:S \Lambda \Rightarrow \mathscr{F},
                    \\quad
                    \\epsilon':Id_{\mathcal{A}}\xRightarrow{\sim}\mathscr{F}
            %p such that
            %p
              (i)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is left derivable;
            %p
              (ii)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
              is right derivable;
            %p
              (iii)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{F}
              preserve cofibrant and fibrant objects;
            %p
              (iv)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta'
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon'
              are natural weak equivalences;
            %p
              (v) If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in\mathcal{T}
              is cofibrant then
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi SX
                      %mi S
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ϵ
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi SX
                      %mi S
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_{SX}S\eta_X\simeq \epsilon'_{SX}S\eta_X'
            %p
              (vi) If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\in\mathcal{A}
              is fibrant then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Λ
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi Y
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mrow
                          %mi Λ
                          %mi Y
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi ϵ
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi Y
                      %mi η
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mrow
                          %mi Λ
                          %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda\epsilon_Y \eta_{\Lambda Y}\simeq \Lambda\epsilon'_Y\eta'_{\Lambda Y}
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{F}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta'
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon'
            are all identities and the homotopy equivalences in (v) and (vi) are equalities we recover the notion of a weak Quillen adjunction. If we further require
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to preserve cofibrations and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            to preserve fibrations we get a Quillen adjunction. Though the above information is weaker than that of a Quillen adjunction it suffices to construct an adjunction at the homotopy categories level.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#VVieira2020"}> Vieira 2020, Theorem 2.1.2
              ) A quasiadjunction induces an adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi o
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo ⇌
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi o
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbb{L}S \dashv\mathbb{R}\Lambda):\mathcal{H}o \mathcal{T}\rightleftharpoons \mathcal{H}o \mathcal{A}
            %p between the homotopy categories.
          %h3#idempotent_quasicomonads Idempotent quasi(co)monads
          %p
            The following generalization of Quillen idempotent monads (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield-Friedlander+theorem"} Bousfield-Friedlander theorem
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#VVieira2020"}> Vieira 2020, Definition 2.3.1
              ) Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              be a right proper model category. A Quillen idempotent quasimonad on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q,\overline{\mathscr{C}}:\mathcal{T}\rightarrow\mathcal{T}
              equipped with a natural span
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                      %mo ¯
                    %mover
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi 𝒯
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta':\overline{\mathscr{C}}\xRightarrow{\sim}Id_{\mathcal{T}}
                    ,\qquad
                    \\eta:\overline{\mathscr{C}}\Rightarrow Q
            %p such that:
            %p
              (i)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta'
              is a natural weak equivalence;
            %p
              (ii)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              preserves weak equivalences;
            %p
              (iii)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q\eta
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_{Q}
              are natural weak equivalences;
            %p
              (iv) If
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in\mathcal{T}(X,B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in F(E,B)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Qf
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_E,\eta_B,Qf\in W
              then
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(f^\ast p)\in W
            %p
              (v) If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
