            %p
          %p The above definition can be dualized. The resulting idempotent quasicomonads induce right Bousfield localizations and associated coreflective homotopy subcategories.
          %h3#idempotent_quasiadjunctions Idempotent quasiadjunctions
          %p
            A quasiadjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %mi Λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒯
                  %mo ⇌
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S\dashv_{\ \mathscr{C},\mathscr{F}}\Lambda):\mathcal{T}\rightleftharpoons \mathcal{A}
            induces the following natural span on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            and natural cospan on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cof
                  %mi η
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mi Cof
                  %mo :
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mi Cof
                  %mover
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo ∼
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Λ
                  %msub
                    %mi fib
                    %mi S
                  %mi η
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cof
                  %mo :
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mi Cof
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi Fib
                  %mi S
                  %mi Cof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  cof \eta'_{Cof}:\mathscr{C} Cof\xRightarrow{\sim} Id_{\mathcal{T}},
                  \\quad
                  (\Lambda fib_S \eta)_{Cof}:\mathscr{C} Cof\Rightarrow \Lambda Fib S Cof
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mi cof
                    %mi Λ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Fib
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mi Cof
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi Fib
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %mi Fib
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi ϵ
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mi Fib
                  %mi fib
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %mover
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo ∼
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %mi Fib
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\epsilon S cof_{\Lambda})_{Fib}: S Cof \Lambda Fib\Rightarrow \mathscr{F} Fib,
                  \\quad
                  \\epsilon'_{Fib}fib:Id_{\mathcal{A}}\xRightarrow{\sim} \mathscr{F} Fib
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cof
                  %mo :
                  %mi Cof
                  %mover
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo ∼
                  %mi Id
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof : Cof \xRightarrow{\sim} Id
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi fib
                  %mo :
                  %mi Id
                  %mover
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo ∼
                  %mi Fib
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} fib : Id \xRightarrow{\sim} Fib
            are the functorial (co)fibrant resolutions of the model structures.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#VVieira2020"}> Vieira 2020, Definition 2.3.7
              ) An idempotent quasiadjunction is a quasiadjunction such that the induced span and cospan are respectively an idempotent quasimonad and an idempotent quasicomonad.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#VVieira2020"}> Vieira 2020, Theorem 2.3.8
              ) An idempotent quasiadjunction induces an equivalence between the associated (co)reflective homotopy subcategories.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
